"""PNRO15 (NRO15): dequant-float matvec (mmvdq) for Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K decode.

Port of nasone32/llama.cpp-RDNA3-7900xtx-opt 67051293 (AMD, Annie Ren):
for ne11 == 1 contiguous, non-batched K-quant matvec, dequantize the weights
to float and dot against the F32 activation instead of quantizing the
activation to Q8_1 first (mmvq). Generated with bigcherry.patch.port_diff
and verified byte-exact against the intended result.

Scope decisions (PNRO15 plan, GPT review):
  * mmvdq.cu/.cuh are FOLDED into mmvq.cu/.cuh -- the patch engine edits
    existing files only;
  * the fused gate+up SwiGLU route of the same commit is NOT wired (its
    kernel is compiled but unreachable) -- a separate, later package;
  * the commit's RDNA3.5 graph-opt default is NOT ported (that is
    PRBE36/1217's scope).
Selection: default on for RDNA3.5 only; GGML_CUDA_DQ_MMV / GGML_CUDA_DQ_Q6K
override (unset = arch default, 0 = off, non-zero = on); GGML_CUDA_DQ_ROWS
tunes rows per block. On gfx1100/gfx1201 it is opt-in.

Activation: BIGCHERRY_PATCH_TRACE=1 logs
  BIGCHERRY_PATCH_HIT patch=1262_nro15 path=mmvdq
"""

